    <activityDescription>
      <activity id="294f21fd-3826-588c-a57a-a25600263b1b" activityNameId="81b64d4a-ea54-51da-8ba4-6397336892fd" activityNameContextId="f44c43c1-5cc5-54a6-ade6-24435bd12c83" type="1" specialActivityType="0" energyValues="0">
        <activityName xml:lang="en">Ground heat exchanger for office buildings, long: 0.667 m</activityName>
        <generalComment>
          <text xml:lang="en" index="1">Full activity name: Ground heat exchanger for office buildings, long: 0.667 m
Production of a ground heat exchanger for an office building with a specific air flow rate of 0.92 m3/h per m2 heated gross floor area. The reference value of the inventory is 1 m2 heated gross floor area. The inventory is based on a study of an appartment building with 6 flats, a heated gross floor area of The inventory is based on a long ground heat exchanger with a specific duct lenght of 0.167m per m3 nominal air flow.  m3/h. The inventory includes a ground heat exchanger with 200mm diameter and a lenght of 0.667m/m2. The data represents a ground heat exchanger made of polyethylene. It includes the excavating needed and a bedding layer made of poor concrete.;
UUID: 2b5b7342-6d00-329e-9798-723f3e053bd2
Materials used for the production. Energy use for the different production steps and for heating the production building. Transport of raw materials to the plant. Estimation for infrastructure of the production site included.
Location: Data sources from one building in Switzerland. Process applicable in central European conditions.
Technology: Typical technology and materials used for ground heat exchangers
Time period: Amount of material investigated in 2003. Process information partly from 2003 to 2008
Production volume: na
Sampling: Data from literature and assumptions concerning example buildings used. 
Extrapolations: none
Uncertainty adjustments: none
BAFU mapped export: unsupported biosphere exchanges excluded; see audit/. Local UUIDs and generic activity classification are export conventions. Source: process_2b5b7342-6d00-329e-9798-723f3e053bd2.xml</text>
        </generalComment>
      </activity>
